%%{init: {'theme': 'dark'}}%%
sequenceDiagram
  participant B as 🌐 Browser (Alice)
  participant S as ⚙️ Server

  rect rgb(20, 30, 50)
    Note over B,S: ── WRITING A CARD ──
    B->>B: 1. generate random DEK (256-bit)
    B->>B: 2. ciphertext = AES-256-GCM(payload, DEK)
    Note left of B: payload = title, description (Markdown),<br/>start_date, due_date, priority,<br/>assignees, labels, checklist,<br/>github_refs
    B->>B: 3. enc_DEK[alice_fp] = OpenPGP.encrypt(DEK, alice_pub)
    B->>B: 3. enc_DEK[bob_fp]   = OpenPGP.encrypt(DEK, bob_pub)
    B->>B: 4. signature = OpenPGP.sign(ciphertext, alice_priv)
    B->>S: POST /cards { workspace_id, column_id, position,<br/>ciphertext, signed_by, signature,<br/>keys: { alice_fp: …, bob_fp: … } }
    Note right of S: Stores opaque blob<br/>Knows: workspace · column · position<br/>Does NOT know: any content
  end

  rect rgb(20, 40, 35)
    Note over B,S: ── READING THE BOARD ──
    B->>S: GET /workspaces/ws_abc/cards
    S-->>B: [ { id, column_id, position, ciphertext, signed_by, keys } ]
    loop for each card
      B->>B: enc_DEK = keys[my_fingerprint]
      B->>B: DEK = OpenPGP.decrypt(enc_DEK, my_priv)
      B->>B: payload = AES-256-GCM-decrypt(ciphertext, DEK)
      B->>B: ✓ verify signature with pubkeys[signed_by]
      B->>B: render card on board
    end
  end
